From a1fd9dfc376f6aee92edd4dd6c69535e3cc4281a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SteveDeFacto <5148995+SteveDeFacto@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 22:42:54 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 13/19] One local Base verifier runtime: gossip head -> roots
 -> gateway -> Helios

network/rpc-runtime.mjs composes the reviewed pieces into one supervised process (entry:
network/rpc-runtime-main.mjs check|run <config>):
  witness-check helper -> root store (pushed heads only) -> head relay and proof-aware witness
  gateway on 127.0.0.1 -> native gossip head source, whose every verified head goes to
  roots.offer first and then to the relay -> Helios, started only after the first fresh verified
  head, ready once its port provably belongs to it, it answers chain 8453 and it reached that head.

No stage needs a proof from an RPC service before its own verifier runs; the upstream proof
sources are explicit, untrusted config, and a failed proof is never replaced by provider
agreement (no fallback inside; consumer rollback is unsetting chainAuthority). Pinned chain,
signer and tested binary builds; binaries copied into a 0700 run directory, hashed and run from
there. One runtime per stateDir. Owned children (recorded identity + staged-exe rule) reaped on the
next start; all-or-nothing startup; ordered shutdown; status.json from head-source start with
honest labels (unsafe head, no finality, not provider-independent, cache = history only).

Tests: config/startup refusals and fan-out order (unit); real Base gossip objects with gaps through
the real native commitment mode and real ancestry headers (no synthetic authority); the composed
processes on A's canonical reth --dev rig with real contracts and a TEST sequencer key (startup
order with every proof source down, lease snapshot, host admission/moderation, admin AddressBook
migration, lying and down sources, missed heads, stale head, whole-operation deadline, crash
reaping, shutdown, failed startups). The reth genesis gains the EIP-2935 history contract Base
has, so Helios's path for blocks it skipped can work (derived fixture, script included).
